notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T10:00:32.043Z","harness:codex",A tag-push Release run currently knows only tag_push in its run name. Do not equate that with the upstream Auto Release trigger; completing the accepted provenance contract needs immutable upstream attribution through the tag or an explicitly dispatched Release workflow without duplicate publish runs.
  "2026-10-10T09:36:49.416Z","harness:codex","Additional owned-temporary native Git acceptance confirms that a missing legacy inventory throws ENOENT and malformed inventory JSON throws SyntaxError before publication; both probes restore their copied inventory. The real tracker and source policy are untouched. Publication admission has no inferred date cutoff, actor inference, external authentication fallback or automatically extended compatibility set. Local tag preparation remains readable context but requires a hosted producer before new hosted publication."
  "2026-10-10T10:08:01.540Z","harness:codex","Recovery topology was rechecked against the full Release workflow: upstream-origin admission executes from reviewed default-branch source before any unpublished exact-tag source checkout. The frozen legacy inventory therefore remains adjacent to its current first-party module, while copied package controls retain their own import topology. Existing npm publication is independently probed and skipped; legacy admission does not authorize republishing different source under an immutable version. The later nine-platform/manager recovery is still pending reviewed-main delivery."
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T10:00:32.723Z","harness:codex","GitHub workflow_dispatch is shared by a local timer and an operator. Count dispatches by a declared origin retained in the run name and attempt receipt, not by event or actor; preserve an explicit historical gap when older runs lack attribution."
  "2026-10-10T09:28:02.731Z","harness:codex","Historical compatibility needs a closed, content-addressed population. A version/date boundary or a non-JSON annotation alone cannot distinguish a new tag from an old one. Bind legacy admission to the exact reviewed repository/tag/object inventory, retain unknown attribution honestly, and prove both allowed recovery and refused unknown/rewritten/local-only tags with real native Git objects. Hosted producer attribution remains a separate independently fetched run/default-branch contract."
  "2026-10-10T13:41:36.317Z","harness:codex","Producer identity is not proof that a run produced a release target: a copied valid run declaration plus an arbitrary descendant passed the earlier source-ancestry check. Independently seal the exact tag name, target commit, tag object and canonical declaration before pushing, then verify the authenticated run artifact before publication. Missing, expired or ambiguous evidence must refuse. The current 90-day retention is an explicit recovery limit; durable producer evidence remains a future concern under this canonical origin owner and must not become a weaker identity-only fallback. Hosted branch advances require a new sealed preparation rather than rebinding an already sealed target."
